# Rendered output. The site is published from a build, not from committed HTML.
/_site/
/.quarto/

# The blackboard PDFs contain every answer, including the in-class problems.
# They render into _site/ (already ignored); this is a belt-and-braces net in
# case anything is ever built in place.
*.pdf

# In-place render output beside the source. `/_site/` above is root-anchored
# and does not catch this: a `quarto preview` session, or a render aimed at a
# directory rather than the project, drops index.html and index_files/ INTO
# lectures/<slug>/. That happened on 2026-08-16 and left 680K of untracked
# build output — safe content, but one `git add -A` from being committed to a
# public repo. The *.pdf net above already anticipated in-place builds; this
# is the same idea for HTML, which it did not cover.
/lectures/*/index.html
/lectures/*/*_files/

# Freeze is disabled in _quarto.yml (see the comment there): its hash ignores
# the in_class symlink, so it silently replays the wrong build in both
# directions, and an instructor build leaves the answers sitting in _freeze/ as
# plain text. Ignored here as a second line of defence in case it is ever
# re-enabled.
/_freeze/

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   in_class     a committed symlink that must keep pointing at for_students/.
#                A fresh clone with a dangling link fails the build outright —
#                including the student HTML — so it cannot be ignored. Local
#                flips to the instructor tree are hidden per-clone with:
#                    git update-index --skip-worktree in_class
#
# The instructor material itself (../for_me) lives outside this repository
# entirely, so there is nothing here to ignore.

**/*.quarto_ipynb

# macOS Finder metadata.
.DS_Store
